@startuml CloudWarehouse_Constraint_Influence
title Key Constraints -> Architectural Outcomes - Bottom
left to right direction
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #34495e
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "Constraints -> Outcomes" {

  rectangle "Constraint\nCourse timeline" as C1 #FFF3E0
  rectangle "Constraint\nSQL Server required" as C2 #FFF3E0
  rectangle "Constraint\nSupplier Excel varies" as C3 #FFF3E0

  rectangle "Outcome\nMonolith + MVP scope" as D1 #ECEFF1
  rectangle "Outcome\nDapper + schema.sql" as D2 #ECEFF1
  rectangle "Outcome\nDual parser + template" as D3 #ECEFF1

  C1 -[#E74C3C,thickness=2]-> D1 : drives
  C2 -[#E74C3C,thickness=2]-> D2 : drives
  C3 -[#E74C3C,thickness=2]-> D3 : drives
}

legend bottom
  **Hard constraints:** .NET 9 + SQL Server | rules by import only | any row error => full rollback
endlegend

@enduml

' 1. External constraints directly shaped our architecture, not optional preferences.
' 2. SQL Server and timeline pushed us to monolith plus Dapper with a hand-written schema.
' 3. Messy supplier Excel drove dual-format parsing and a downloadable standard template.
